{"publication":"24594","pdfSha256":"e18bd39ad0ca19d2eb9b9ea25c2635144c5ab368e5d6fbdc7a08345515ea1aee","pdfPage":266,"layoutPage":"                                        [AMD Public Use]\n\nAMD64 Technology                                                        24594—Rev. 3.38—July 2026\n\n\n\nInstruction Encoding\n\nMnemonic                                                                 Encoding\n                                                    XOP    RXB.map_select       W.vvvv.L.pp      Opcode\nLLWPCB reg32                                       8F      RXB.09              0.1111.0.00      12 /0\nLLWPCB reg64                                       8F      RXB.09              1.1111.0.00      12 /0\n\nModRM.reg augments the opcode and is assigned the value 0. ModRM.r/m (augmented by XOP.R)\nspecifies the register containing the effective address of the LWPCB. ModRM.mod is 11b.\n\nRelated Instructions\nSLWPCB, LWPVAL, LWPINS\n\nrFLAGS Affected\nNone\n\nExceptions\n                           Virtual\n      Exception                                                 Cause of Exception\n                      Real 8086 Protected\n                                            LWP instructions are not supported, as indicated by CPUID\n                       X    X       X\nInvalid opcode,                             Fn8000_0001_ECX[LWP] = 0.\n#UD                    X    X               The system is not in protected mode.\n                                    X       LWP is not available, or mod != 11b, or vvvv != 1111b.\n                                            Any part of the LWPCB or the event ring buffer is beyond the\nGeneral protection,                 X\n                                            DS segment limit.\n#GP\n                                    X       Any restrictions on the contents of the LWPCB are violated\n                                    X       A page fault resulted from reading or writing the LWPCB.\n                                            LWP was already enabled and a page fault resulted from\n                                    X\nPage fault, #PF                             reading or writing the old LWPCB.\n                                            LWP was already enabled and a page fault resulted from\n                                    X\n                                            flushing an event to the old ring buffer.\n\n\n\n\n224                                                                                   General-Purpose\n                                                                                 Instruction Reference\n","cells":[{"id":"pdf:266:cell:0","pdfPage":266,"rect":[251.151489,4.09422,360.846489,23.20422],"wordSpan":[0,3],"wordBoxesSha256":"ed9e5522e2d0355c23d3fc390d480afdc96221e75c81b889abc30b06c4ed7943","unicodeSha256":"cb9a32cb7cda694a9471249208941a694cc0a803969c2bac64dd553086c94897","text":"[AMD Public Use]","wordBoxes":[{"text":"[AMD","rect":[251.151489,4.09422,286.151489,23.20422]},{"text":"Public","rect":[290.041489,4.09422,328.163489,23.20422]},{"text":"Use]","rect":[332.062489,4.09422,360.846489,23.20422]}],"glyphSpan":null,"glyphEvidence":"not-extracted: source is Unicode word boxes"},{"id":"pdf:266:cell:1","pdfPage":266,"rect":[62.9984,45.6171,164.6362,60.9511],"wordSpan":[3,5],"wordBoxesSha256":"3b691e873427ef161dd8ef6ee5cb83ed75dd4effe4711a4de873ded3f578f2ab","unicodeSha256":"70e213c4a31748f9f77a863ce4e1e49ee9ff8122a32f47b46615b19d2f2bc8c7","text":"AMD64 Technology","wordBoxes":[{"text":"AMD64","rect":[62.9984,45.6171,100.3126,60.9511]},{"text":"Technology","rect":[103.3167,45.6171,164.6362,60.9511]}],"glyphSpan":null,"glyphEvidence":"not-extracted: source is Unicode word boxes"},{"id":"pdf:266:cell:2","pdfPage":266,"rect":[399.9834,45.6171,549.0994,60.9511],"wordSpan":[5,8],"wordBoxesSha256":"78c55caa48ae49c2659f518081fe1d4be8444efc89f137deefc1de65b3c0c395","unicodeSha256":"aaf564d78c1add333e5bd48fe8c3a2f7cbdc1f6bf77a0a5898e45dd31c057d08","text":"24594—